   "date": "2017-11-08T03:52:29Z",
   "subject": "2B-PLS question",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small\">Hi geomorphers!</div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small\">I am interested in using integration methods such as 2B-PLS on shape data from 4 different taxa with intraspecific variation. I was able to successfully run 2B-PLS in geomorph considering all data points as independent. However, I am wondering if there is a way to consider the group structure in the analysis. In other words, I was able to produce a best fit line by simply plotting my 2B-PLS results, but is there a way to consider that my taxonomic groups might be following different patterns of integration? Any help would be greatly appreciated!</div><br clear=\"all\" style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small\"><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small\"><div class=\"gmail_signature\" data-smartmail=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">Best,</font><div><font size=\"2\" face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">Angie Peña</font></div></div></div></div></div></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "oX1xc3hlCwAJ",
   "from": "Emma Sherratt",
