   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small\">Emma,</span><div><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small\">Thank you for your response! I&#39;m not necessarily looking to use phylogenetic methods, but I am wondering if it&#39;s possible to plot fit lines for each of my groups in the analysis and compare the slopes and intercepts of each group, like in a regular regression. Is it possible to evaluate patterns of integration this way using 2B-PLS?</span></div><div><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">- Angie<br></font></div></div>"
